# One 259-char shell one-liner inside a block scalar (bunkerweb mariadb dump
# invocation). Breaking it would change the rendered dump script that is
# byte-reconciled against live citadel; not worth the churn.
# Moved here from roles/borgmatic_citadel/defaults/main.yml when the two
# per-host borgmatic roles merged into roles/borgmatic: borgmatic_databases is
# per-host data, so it now lives in host_vars. This path is matched literally,
# so a stale entry fails silently (the rule just starts firing at the new
# location) rather than erroring.
# Moved again when citadel's host_vars became a directory to carry a vault.yml
# alongside (bunkerweb_stack secrets).
inventory/host_vars/citadel/vars.yml yaml[line-length]

# roles/compose_stack sources are byte-faithful captures of live compose
# files; reformatting any of them would break the cmp reconciliation against
# the running host. Style loses to fidelity here, same doctrine as the
# bunkerweb template.
roles/compose_stack/files/warrig/immich/docker-compose.yml yaml[line-length]
roles/compose_stack/files/warrig/metube/docker-compose.yml yaml[line-length]
roles/compose_stack/files/warrig/webhooksite/docker-compose.yml yaml[indentation]
